╭─ Use eza for ls? ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Oh My Shell does not read the aliases of fish or bash, so `ls` runs the    │
│ system ls. eza is on your PATH.                                            │
│ Choosing it writes ui.ls = "eza" to config.toml, and `ls` runs eza from    │
│ now on. To undo it: Ctrl+P, Settings, ui.ls, or `unalias ls` for one       │
│ session.                                                                   │
│                                                                            │
│ [⟨4⟩U⟨0⟩se eza for ls]  ⟨7⟩ ⟨0⟩⟨4;7⟩N⟨0⟩⟨7⟩ot now ⟨0⟩                                                │
╰─ ←→ move⟨2⟩ · ⟨0⟩Enter choose⟨2⟩ · ⟨0⟩Esc not now ─────────────────────────────────────╯
